# Treat Unity serialized YAML as binary for line-ending purposes so they don't show as
# perpetually "modified" (phantom diffs that block git pull). Unity always writes LF.
# merge=unityyamlmerge uses Unity's Smart Merge tool (UnityYAMLMerge) to merge scenes/prefabs
# safely instead of corrupting them. Configure the driver once per machine (see docs/AI_WORKFLOW.md):
#   git config merge.unityyamlmerge.driver '"<UnityEditor>/Data/Tools/UnityYAMLMerge.exe" merge -p %O %B %A %A'
#
# -whitespace: Unity ALWAYS writes a trailing space after an empty YAML field ("userData: ",
# "m_Name: ", "assetBundleName: "). git diff --check honours the `whitespace` attribute, and
# `-text` alone does not disable it - so without this, EVERY commit that adds or edits a Unity
# asset fails Fast Preflight's "Commit whitespace and conflict check". It is not a style problem
# we can fix: stripping the spaces means fighting the editor forever, and it rewrites them on the
# next save. Measured: the pre-API-updater snapshot 93cf8cd1 tripped it 11,080 times.
# The check keeps its real job - catching trailing whitespace in HAND-written .cs/.md/.py/.ps1.
*.unity   -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.prefab  -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.asset   -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.controller -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.anim    -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.mat     -text -whitespace merge=unityyamlmerge
*.meta    -text -whitespace
*.asmdef  -text -whitespace

# Normal text files
*.cs   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
# ...except the AI's own plan artifacts, which THE_RATCHET.md R1 requires we keep VERBATIM as
# evidence. We do not get to tidy them, so they do not get whitespace-checked either.
# (_ZIPTIDE_HOUSE_RULES.md is ours and is deliberately NOT exempted - it is held to the normal bar.)
Ziptide/Assets/Plans/*.md -whitespace
Ziptide/Assets/Plans/_ZIPTIDE_HOUSE_RULES.md whitespace
*.json text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# ── Pseudo-binary Unity assets (V2 Q5 / Terry's PDF §Version Control): these LOOK like YAML but
#    carry packed data — ANY text-based merge corrupts them permanently. More-specific patterns
#    override the *.asset smart-merge rule above.
*[Tt]errain.asset binary
*[Nn]av[Mm]esh.asset binary
LightingData.asset binary

# ── True binaries (explicit, so no future tool tries to diff/normalize them) ──────────────────
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.fbx binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.dll binary
*.apk binary

